{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReinsertRow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReinsertRow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedAddable","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCornersAlong"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowIndices_uninsertSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowIndices_uninsertSteps","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L176-L191","doc":"**The recovered word records the positions it was recovered from.**\n\nOne step of `newRowIndex_uninsert` wrapped around the inductive hypothesis, with brick 10 collapsing\nthe intermediate tableau back to the one the hypothesis is stated at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.newRowIndex_uninsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.newRowIndex_uninsert","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L151-L174","doc":"**The re-inserted letter goes back to the row it was peeled from.**\n\nBrick 10 said `insert (uninsert T i).1 z = T`; this says the cell that rebuilt `T` is the cell at\nrow `i`. The argument is entirely at the level of shapes: the peel takes the shape to\n`removeCorner`, the re-insertion takes it back by `addCell` at whatever row it chose, and `addCell`\nhas only one index that lands on the shape you started from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell_index_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell_index_inj","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L141-L149","doc":"**`addCell` determines its index.** It moves exactly one entry, so two legal indices producing\nthe same shape are the same index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.le_length_removeCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.le_length_removeCorner","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L131-L139","doc":"The peeled index is still a legal position in the peeled shape — needed to compare it with the\nindex the re-insertion chose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell_removeCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell_removeCorner","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L115-L129","doc":"**Adding the cell back at a corner returns the shape.** The exact inverse of `removeCorner`, in\nthe direction the RSK inverse needs: the peel is undone by the re-insertion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCorner_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCorner_eq","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L83-L113","doc":"**The anatomy of `removeCorner` on a Young shape.** Either the row keeps a cell, in which case\nthe zero-filter is inert and the operation is a plain `set`; or the row had a single cell, in which\ncase the corner condition forces it to be the last row and the filter deletes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_set_or_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_set_or_eq","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L67-L81","doc":"A member of a `set` list is a member of the original or the written value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.take_append_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.take_append_last","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L54-L65","doc":"Reading the final entry back off the prefix reassembles the list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.set_last_eq_take","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.set_last_eq_take","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedReinsertRow.lean#L41-L52","doc":"Setting the final entry rewrites the list as its prefix with that entry replaced. ","signatureChunk":0}]}